WEBVTT

NOTE Cues sit near the top (line:4%) so they don't cover on-screen labels.

1a-1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.801 line:4% align:center
Scores tell a business where it stands.

1a-2
00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:05.160 line:4% align:center
Recommendations suggest what to do next.

1b-1
00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:08.750 line:4% align:center
So what does the AI actually see when it writes them?

2a-1
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:11.936 line:4% align:center
For recommendations, the application first

2a-2
00:00:11.936 --> 00:00:14.707 line:4% align:center
calculates the scores. The model receives those

2a-3
00:00:14.707 --> 00:00:16.770 line:4% align:center
results; it doesn’t calculate them.

2b-1
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.032 line:4% align:center
The application builds one request, in code,

2b-2
00:00:20.032 --> 00:00:21.080 line:4% align:center
with four parts:

2c-1
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:25.198 line:4% align:center
context, answers and scores, selected evidence,

2c-2
00:00:25.198 --> 00:00:26.630 line:4% align:center
and instructions.

3a-1
00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:29.980 line:4% align:center
First, the context of our fictional food

3a-2
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.851 line:4% align:center
business in Peru. Then its answers, and the

3a-3
00:00:32.851 --> 00:00:34.720 line:4% align:center
scores calculated from them.

4a-1
00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:36.820 line:4% align:center
Next, the evidence.

4b-1
00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:40.074 line:4% align:center
Without reference material, an AI model relies

4b-2
00:00:40.074 --> 00:00:42.900 line:4% align:center
on patterns learned during training. It can

4b-3
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:46.055 line:4% align:center
produce convincing answers that contain mistakes

4b-4
00:00:46.055 --> 00:00:47.370 line:4% align:center
or invented details.

4c-1
00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:51.430 line:4% align:center
MOSAIC uses retrieval-augmented generation, or

4c-2
00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:55.051 line:4% align:center
RAG. Think of it as giving the model a reference

4c-3
00:00:55.051 --> 00:00:57.390 line:4% align:center
pack before asking it to write.

4d-1
00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.525 line:4% align:center
The application selects passages from MOSAIC’s

4d-2
00:01:00.525 --> 00:01:03.025 line:4% align:center
knowledge base using rules that match the

4d-3
00:01:03.025 --> 00:01:05.952 line:4% align:center
business’s context and relevant topics. It sends

4d-4
00:01:05.952 --> 00:01:08.818 line:4% align:center
those passages alongside the business’s answers

4d-5
00:01:08.818 --> 00:01:10.160 line:4% align:center
and calculated scores.

4e-1
00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:13.186 line:4% align:center
The model is instructed to use that evidence and

4e-2
00:01:13.186 --> 00:01:15.849 line:4% align:center
cite its sources. This is intended to reduce

4e-3
00:01:15.849 --> 00:01:18.634 line:4% align:center
unsupported claims and makes the advice easier

4e-4
00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:21.600 line:4% align:center
to check, although it doesn’t guarantee accuracy.

4f-1
00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:26.057 line:4% align:center
Because the selection follows rules, it can be

4f-2
00:01:26.057 --> 00:01:28.180 line:4% align:center
inspected and repeated.

4g-1
00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:31.023 line:4% align:center
Keeping the reference pack focused controls

4g-2
00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:34.028 line:4% align:center
processing costs. A separate review is needed to

4g-3
00:01:34.028 --> 00:01:37.660 line:4% align:center
check whether the selection leaves out important guidance.

5a-1
00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.460 line:4% align:center
Last, the instructions.

5b-1
00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:43.413 line:4% align:center
Start from the business’s actual answers, then

5b-2
00:01:43.413 --> 00:01:46.520 line:4% align:center
the evidence, and use the scores to set priorities.

5c-1
00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:49.375 line:4% align:center
Keep every recommendation realistic for a

5c-2
00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:50.710 line:4% align:center
company of this size.

5d-1
00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.669 line:4% align:center
Don’t introduce laws, standards or numeric

5d-2
00:01:53.669 --> 00:01:56.135 line:4% align:center
thresholds unless the retrieved evidence

5d-3
00:01:56.135 --> 00:01:58.785 line:4% align:center
supports them, and cite the source for each

5d-4
00:01:58.785 --> 00:01:59.710 line:4% align:center
recommendation.

6a-1
00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:03.176 line:4% align:center
The model returns a structured result: a short

6a-2
00:02:03.176 --> 00:02:05.962 line:4% align:center
summary, up to five recommendations, and up to

6a-3
00:02:05.962 --> 00:02:06.870 line:4% align:center
three key gaps.

6b-1
00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:09.491 line:4% align:center
Here’s one, from a saved result for this

6b-2
00:02:09.491 --> 00:02:13.030 line:4% align:center
business: put in place basic waste and packaging measurement.

6c-1
00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:16.392 line:4% align:center
It starts from what the business reported: waste

6c-2
00:02:16.392 --> 00:02:18.856 line:4% align:center
isn’t tracked, and packaging isn’t yet

6c-3
00:02:18.856 --> 00:02:21.320 line:4% align:center
eco-friendly. And it names its source.

7a-1
00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:23.070 line:4% align:center
Then the checks.

7b-1
00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:26.038 line:4% align:center
Automated checks test the expected structure and

7b-2
00:02:26.038 --> 00:02:28.354 line:4% align:center
source references. Assessing whether the

7b-3
00:02:28.354 --> 00:02:31.132 line:4% align:center
evidence supports the advice requires a separate

7b-4
00:02:31.132 --> 00:02:32.000 line:4% align:center
quality review.

8a-1
00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.206 line:4% align:center
MOSAIC controls the calculation, the evidence

8a-2
00:02:36.206 --> 00:02:39.092 line:4% align:center
selection and the request. The model supplies

8a-3
00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:40.310 line:4% align:center
the interpretation.

8b-1
00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:42.851 line:4% align:center
The same inputs, configuration and

8b-2
00:02:42.851 --> 00:02:45.845 line:4% align:center
knowledge-base version produce the same evidence

8b-3
00:02:45.845 --> 00:02:48.776 line:4% align:center
selection and request construction. The wording

8b-4
00:02:48.776 --> 00:02:52.020 line:4% align:center
of the advice can vary; the scores beneath it don’t.

9a-1
00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:55.460 line:4% align:center
MOSAIC. The pieces that matter.
